cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI for Renewable Energy Systems — Applied Research Portfolio"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Murat
    family-names: Kus
abstract: >-
  Six engineering research projects applying reinforcement learning, model
  predictive control and probabilistic forecasting to the German electricity
  system: prosumer PV and battery energy management at 15-minute resolution,
  multi-market pumped-storage dispatch, smart EV charging under grid-orientated
  control, energy sharing in renewable energy communities, utility-scale hybrid
  wind-PV-battery plant dispatch, and probabilistic forecast-to-bid intraday
  trading. Each project treats the German regulatory framework as part of the
  environment specification and evaluates learned controllers against a
  deployable rolling-horizon MILP-MPC baseline.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - model predictive control
  - energy systems
  - electricity markets
  - renewable energy
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - German energy regulation
  - battery storage
  - pumped storage
  - smart charging
